   "record": "https://github.com/KD5UJC-XYZ/scarab/issues/796",
   "note": "its private parser reads a message as one generic term and checks it afterwards, where decodeMsg reads the list length and key and checks (key, length) before reading on, so a malformed message can be refused at another item and with other text (#796). As the reference since #1029: a refusal's reason is read as decodeRefuseReason reads it, its length read and ignored; generic terms and strings have no depth, count or size cap, only the message's 5760 bytes on receipt (runDecoderWithLimit); the encoder writes a message of any size, as encodeMsg does and the driver sends it (sendMessage, Driver/Limits.hs:109-117); a term keeps an indefinite string's chunks and is written as cborg 0.2.10.0's encodeTerm writes it; and a simple value after 0xf8 is read whatever its value, as decodeTerm reads it",
   "digest": "6081cc83eb8aecd1"
  },
